                <h2 id=3D"tips-from-the-expert-1">Tips from the expert</h2>



                <ul>

                    <li>Regularly audit and rotate API keys and secrets: Re=
duce the risk of key leakage by automating the rotation of API keys and sec=
rets, and conducting regular audits.</li>

                    <li>Implement behavior-based API monitoring: Use machin=
e learning to identify and respond to unusual API usage patterns in real-ti=
me, improving detection of emerging threats.</li>

                    <li>Employ a zero trust model for API access: Ensure th=
at every API request, whether internal or external, is verified before gran=
ting access, reducing the risk of unauthorized access.</li>

                    <li>Integrate API security into DevSecOps: Incorporate =
security checks into your CI/CD pipelines, ensuring that APIs are tested fo=
r vulnerabilities at every stage of development.</li>

                    <li>Apply data masking for sensitive information: Mask =
sensitive data in API responses to reduce the risk of data exposure if an e=
ndpoint is compromised.</li>

                </ul>

